|~ `::holds`, the kind of an invariant, and the laws declared under it.

   The decisions it exists for: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:holds
  |~~ An invariant is a query the values of a kind keep, a quote under
      this tag, written by `holds` in the chain that builds the kind or
      the function it guards and laid under the name of the refusal of a
      value that breaks it: a kind of
      `(::kind | holds :TooLargeError |~~ Below ten. ~~| ~(lt 10))`
      declared as `:Small` refuses `::Small#12` under
      `::Small/TooLargeError`.

      An invariant guards the value of a kind or a field of its payload,
      and an input or the answer of a function, by the path of its name,
      and runs when the value is built, read or answered, an invariant of
      a kind's value on the payload beneath the tag, so a word in it that
      keeps its subject's kind runs over no tag, `~(eq (sort))`; the kinds of a
      value are named where it is taken, `| takes :by … ::number`, and
      no invariant asks them. Declared by a name outside a chain, an
      invariant holds of nothing and is refused.
      ::link~(::kind/holds | doc) ::link~(::fn/holds | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang/verbs | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | proves :readsThePayloadBeneathTheTag
        |~~ An invariant of a kind's value reads the payload beneath the
            tag, so a word that keeps its subject's kind runs in it.
        ~~|
        ~(:Sorted |~~ In order. ~~| (::kind | holds :NotSortedError |~~ In order. ~~| ~(eq (sort))) | get [~(::Sorted[1 2] | payload) ~(::Sorted[2 1] !| type)] | eq [[1 2] ::Sorted/NotSortedError])
    | proves :refusesUnderItsName
        |~~ A value that breaks an invariant is refused under its name. ~~|
        ~(:Small |~~ Below ten. ~~| (::kind | holds :TooLargeError |~~ A number below ten. ~~| ~(lt 10)) | get [~(::Small#3 | type) ~(::Small#12 !| type)] | eq [::Small ::Small/TooLargeError])

